 "title": "Assessor's Office - Ringgold County Government - Iowa",
 "text": "Assessor's Office - Ringgold County Government - Iowa\nSkip to content\nWelcome to the new Ringgold County website!\nSearch\nAbout\nBoards & Commissions\nCemeteries\nCommunities\nElected Officials\nSchool Districts\nTownship Information\nDepartments\nAssessor\nAttorney\nAuditor\nBoard of Supervisors\nClerk of Court\nConservation\nE911\nEmergency Management\nGeneral Assistance\nPublic Health\nRCSS\nRecorder\nSecondary Roads\nSheriff\nTreasurer\nVeterans Affairs\nResources\nBid Notices\nCalendar\nFrequently Asked Questions\nJob Opportunities\nNews\nNotifications\nWRD Landfill\nContact\nWebsite Search\nType 2 or more characters for results.\nDepartments\nAssessor\nLocation\n109 W Madison\nMount Ayr, IA 50854\nDriving Directions\nContact Information\n641-464-3233\nmengland@ringgoldcounty.us\nHours\nMonday - Friday\n8:00 am - 4:00 pm\nHoliday Closures\nOur Team\nMelinda England\nAssessor\nRobbie Mason\nChief Deputy Assessor\nStephanie Purdy\nClerk\nBeacon\nBoards\nCredits and Exemptions\nDates to Remember\nProperty Taxation\nProtest of Assessment\nVanguard Data Website\nFAQ\nThe primary duty and responsibility of the assessor is to measure, list, and value all real property within his/her jurisdiction except that which is otherwise provided for by law. The assessor's responsibilities fall under the direction of the Iowa Department of Revenue. The statutory date of assessment is January 1st. The assessor determines a full or partial value of new construction or improvements, depending upon the state of completion as of January 1st.\nCourthouse\n109 W. Madison St.\nMount Ayr, IA 50854\nContact Us\nHours\nM-F 8:00 am to 4:00 pm\nDepartment Hours May Vary Closed Holidays\n©2026 Ringgold County, Iowa | Accessibility\npowered by\nUpcoming Holiday Closure Schedule\nVeterans Day (November 11, 2026)\nThanksgiving (November 26, 2026)\nThanksgiving (November 27, 2026)\nChristmas Eve (December 24, 2026)\nChristmas Day (December 25, 2026)\nNew Year's (January 1, 2027)",
